{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalCornerTrace","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramCornerReindex"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_of_corner_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_of_corner_identity","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/MarkovAssembly.lean#L60-L134","doc":"**The Markov condition, modulo the corner identity.**  For any weight function `w` satisfying\nthe per-corner identity, the `w`-weighted seminormal trace of `ι y · σ_{m+1}` over the diagrams of\nsize `m + 2` is `z` times the `w`-weighted trace of `y` over those of size `m + 1`.\n\nThe proof is the three steps the bean names: decompose each block trace over corners\n(`trace_heckeIncl_mul_lastGen_corner`), reindex the resulting double sum\n(`sum_corner_eq_sum_addable`), then swap the inner sums so the corner identity applies at\n`r = ` the cell carrying each downstairs tableau's top entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.isCornerCell_cellOf_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.isCornerCell_cellOf_card","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/MarkovAssembly.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The cell carrying a tableau's top entry is a removable corner. ","signatureChunk":0}]}